# Set the operating mode of a kitbag sensor.
#
# The namespace's only service. It is here because request and response
# are separate definitions that generate separate types, and a build
# integration that emits only one of them -- or that collides their
# names -- is broken in a way no message-only cell would reveal.
#
# The request is @sealed: it is three bytes issued from a control loop
# and its size is part of the contract. The response is delimited,
# because it is read by tooling that tolerates the type growing in a
# later minor version.

kitbag.Mode.1.0 mode
# Mode to switch to. FAULT is not a valid request and is rejected.

uint8 channel_mask
# Bitmask of channels the new mode applies to. Zero means all of them.

@assert _offset_.max == 16
# Two bytes. Asserted rather than assumed: the request is issued from a
# real-time loop and a silent size change would be a contract change.

@sealed

---

bool accepted
# True when the sensor has adopted the requested mode.

void7
# Padding to a byte boundary.

kitbag.Mode.1.0 mode
# Mode actually in effect after the request, which differs from the
# requested one when the request was rejected.

uint8[<=24] detail
# Optional human-readable reason, UTF-8. Empty on success.

@extent 64 * 8
